# Release lent parameters: `weight` only reads `f`, so its summary keeps
# nothing and `total` passes `f` with no count on either side. `remember`
# stores `f`, so `collect` still counts a copy for it. `apply` calls
# `weight` through a function value: the value's caller passes `f` owned,
# and the adapter releases it after the call. `set_first` keeps nothing,
# but `pinned` passes it a reference into `xs` beside `xs`, so
# `xs` is copied for the call. `weight` has more than 16 instructions, so
# a release build leaves it a call.
